  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Banana Ball is a fast-paced, highly entertaining version of baseball created by the Savannah Bananas, designed to make the sport fun and fan-focused. It features unique rules like two-hour time limits, no bunting, and fans catching foul balls for outs. The game, often called the “Harlem Globetrotters of baseball,” combines high-level competition with performances. Key Rules of Banana Ball Points-Based Scoring: Every inning is worth a point, rather than just cumulative runs. Fan Outs: If a fan catches a foul ball, the batter is out. No Bunting: Bunting is not allowed, which keeps the game action-packed. Two-Hour Time Limit: Games are designed to be played quickly. One-on-One Showdown: If the game is tied, it is decided by a one-on-one competition between a hitter and a pitcher. Stealing First: Batters can attempt to steal first base during a pitch. The Savannah BananasThe team, owned by Fans First Entertainment, has become a viral sensation and plays against opponents like the Party Animals. They are known for their on-field dances, characters, and high-energy performances, garnering a larger social media footprint than many MLB teams. The Bananas play a nationwide tour. Banana Ball Tour and Impact Ticket Lottery: Tickets are notoriously hard to get, requiring fans to join a ticket lottery to attend games. 2026 Tour: The 2026 Banana Ball tour includes games at major stadiums like First Horizon Park and the Caesars Superdome. Player Salaries: Players are professional athletes, with many earning roughly $100,000 annually, which is significantly more than most minor league players. This video explains the misconception that Banana Ball is scripted:00:47Jesse ColeLinkedIn• Feb 18, 2025",
